["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"entity-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0cab7-1ed7-77a5-8384-ff10c92e7ad6","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIGdd694cdee925366106b7eb7f65806f9e6d9c7110638c9d0a787972e3586938d7","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/recorded-command-contract","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nOnly execute exposes envelope flags, partial sets are silently discarded, timestamps are not validated consistently and stored commands currently commit bare events.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nStored create and execute require a record id, valid recorded time and explicit actor choice, preserve optional correlation and causation, print the committed record in the selected format and reject incomplete invocation with exit 2.\n\n## Implementation evidence\n\nMoved to implemented on 2026-09-09 after an audit of every non-implemented artifact against `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/roadmap.md` and the crates.\n\nStored `entity create` and `entity execute` require `--record-id`, a valid `--recorded-at` and exactly one of `--actor`/`--no-actor`; the record printed is the record committed — `CHANGELOG.md` `## [0.15.0]` Changed; since the 2026-09-08 review both verbs run through `entity_shell::StoredRuntime`.\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:the-shell"},{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Create and execute commit the exact record they print and reject partial provenance.","title":"Stored CLI commands require complete recording metadata"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIGdd694cdee925366106b7eb7f65806f9e6d9c7110638c9d0a787972e3586938d7","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIGdd694cdee92536